# Cloudflare Pages - HTTP Headers Configuration
#
# Caching rule of thumb:
#   - /assets/* is generated by Vite with a content hash in every file name, so it can be
#     cached forever ("immutable").
#   - Everything else keeps the same URL when its content changes (CV PDF, og-image, icons,
#     legacy site...), so it must be revalidated. Marking those "immutable" leaves returning
#     visitors with a stale copy (e.g. an outdated CV) for up to a year.
#   - Do not set Cache-Control on two rules that can match the same URL: Pages concatenates
#     the values and the result is contradictory.

# Hashed build output (JS, CSS, and any image or font imported by the app)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# PDF Files - Critical for PDF viewer. Always revalidate so an updated CV is picked up.
/*.pdf
  Content-Type: application/pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Legacy folder (all files)
/legacy/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Web Manifest
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# JSON files
/*.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Text files
/*.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Markdown twins of the resume pages (served as Markdown, readable in a browser tab too)
/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# XML files
/*.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# JavaScript and CSS (bundled assets)
/assets/*.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8

/assets/*.css
  Content-Type: text/css; charset=utf-8

# HTML files - No cache for SPA
/*.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Security headers.
#   - The pages are served at "/", "/resume/" and so on. Pages answers /index.html with a redirect to "/",
#     so a rule written for /index.html never applies (the old one here never did).
#   - Pages joins the values of every rule that matches, so each header below is set by one rule, or by
#     rules that cannot match the same address. Pages already adds X-Content-Type-Options and Referrer-Policy.
#   - No Content-Security-Policy yet: index.html has an inline script and the CV viewer loads PDF.js from a
#     CDN, so a policy needs its own testing (report-only first).
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

# X-Frame-Options only means something for HTML pages, so it sits on the page addresses (the home page,
# every address that ends in a slash, /privacy) and not on PDFs and images. SAMEORIGIN, because the app
# frames the old site (/legacy/) and PDFs from this origin.
/
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/*/
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/privacy
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
